<title>ISRAEL: Israel grain, meal, soy arrivals detailed.</title>
<headline>Israel grain, meal, soy arrivals detailed.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1997-04-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following shipments of grain have arrived or are due to arrive in Israeli ports, according to the inspection agency Hevra Klalit Lehashgaha (in tonnes):</p>
<p>Vessel	     ETA	   Cargo	    Quantity   Origin</p>
<p>Volgobalt 133    unloading   feed wheat	2,753     Europe</p>
<p>Intrepid	   28/4	  wheat	    13,780     Argentina</p>
<p>Liberty Sea	arrived     wheat	    19,120     U.S.</p>
<p>				     sorghum	   9,386</p>
<p>				     soya	     32,465</p>
<p>Liberty Spirit   29/4	  wheat	    38,300     U.S.</p>
<p>				     sorghum	  23,034</p>
<p>Amour		29/4	  maize grits     2,900     Europe</p>
<p>Auk		  10/5	  sunflower meal 53,000     U.S.</p>
<p>				     + corn + wheat</p>
<p>Europa	     24/5	  corn + barley+ 50,000     U.S.</p>
<p>				     sunflower meal</p>
<p>Bora Mete	  28/4	  maize grits     3,100     U.S.</p>
<p>Liberty Sun	20/5	  tbn		61,000     U.S.</p>
<p>Gencis K	   26/5	  gluten feed +  50,000     U.S.</p>
<p>				     gluten meal +</p>
<p>				     sorghum + soya</p>
</text>
